    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "New York City",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S6463\n\nSPONSOR: MYRIE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to authorize the city of New York to establish\nan electronic voter registration transmittal system for New York city\nresidents; and providing for the repeal of such provisions upon expira-\ntion thereof\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis bill would authorize a New York City municipal agency to establish\nan electronic voter registration transmittal system for New York City\nresidents, consistent with local law, until ninety days after the Board\nof Elections of the State of New York establishes, and makes accessible\nto residents of the city of New York, a statewide electronic voter\nregistration transmittal system pursuant to Title 8 of Article 5 of the\nElection Law as added by Part CCC of Chapter 55 of the laws of 2019.\n\n \nREASONS FOR SUPPORT:\n\nThis bill clarifies New York City's authority to create an online voter\nregistration system for the City's residents in advance of the statewide\nonline voter registration system to be established by the State Board of\nElections in 2021 at the latest. In 2017, New York City enacted a local\nlaw that mandated the creation of a system that will allow City resi-\ndents to complete a voter registration form through a website or mobile\napplication. This bill would ensure that the local law could be imple-\nmented in 2019, and that forms generated as a result of the City system\ncould be transmitted electronically to the City's Board of Elections.\nOnline voter registration makes registering to vote more convenient and\naccessible, and this bill would enable New York City residents to take\nadvantage of this important reform ahead of the 2020 presidential\nelection when voter registration rates typically increase. When the\nState Board of Elections implements its statewide online voter registra-\ntion system in 2021 or earlier, the bill would phase out the City's\nsystem.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n",
